<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Publius Quinctilius Varus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Publius Quinctilius Varus was a Roman general and governor. In 9 CE his three legions were ambushed and destroyed by Germanic tribes under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arminius">Arminius</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutoburg-forest">Teutoburg Forest</a>. The defeat ended Roman attempts to conquer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germania">Germania</a> and fixed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>'s northern frontier along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/publius-quinctilius-varus.jpg" alt="Publius Quinctilius Varus" width="252" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Varus_-_Antiquitates_Germanic%C3%A6_-_Tacitus_%26_Hooft.tiff" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
